# The Ghost original signs off with an explicit line break
# ('Sincerely, <br />' then the team name); Medium's importer turned it
# into the same doubled break it uses for wrapped source lines, which
# convert collapses to a space for Ghost-migrated posts. Make it a
# single break in the export and the page's rendered DOM, so the
# signature keeps its own line whichever body source converts. The
# page's stored editor-state copy is left untouched: its markup
# offsets index into the stored text, so editing it would skew them.
file: b79bfd18566d/export.html
old: Sincerely,<br><br>
new: Sincerely,<br>

file: b79bfd18566d/page.html
old: Sincerely,<br/><br/>
new: Sincerely,<br/>
